IO-09: read an outfall's Gated column also when a RouteTo column follows it

outfall_readParams() parsed the Gated token only when it was the last token
on the line (ntoks == n) and the RouteTo subcatchment only when exactly one
more token followed (ntoks == n+1). A line with both, such as
"O1 99 FIXED 102 YES S1", therefore never looked at the Gated token: the flap
gate stayed at its default NO, and any text in that column was accepted.
Test the token count with >= so each optional column is read whenever it is
present.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-09_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/node.c b/src/legacy/engine/node.c
index 070db5a..666ff50 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/node.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/node.c
@@ -1375,14 +1375,14 @@ int outfall_readParams(int j, int k, char* tok[], int ntoks)
           Tseries[m].refersTo = TIMESERIES_OUTFALL;
         }
     }
-    if ( ntoks == n )
+    if ( ntoks >= n )
     {
         m = findmatch(tok[n-1], NoYesWords);               // flap gate
         if ( m < 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_KEYWORD, tok[n-1]);
         x[5] = m;
     }
 
-    if ( ntoks == n+1)
+    if ( ntoks >= n+1 )
     {
         m = project_findObject(SUBCATCH, tok[n]);
         if ( m < 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_NAME, tok[n]);
